- How would you extend to Unicode or larger alphabets while preserving performance?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to blend BFS intuition with shortest-path techniques under a hop constraint and to reconstruct a path from augmented state.

## Key Concepts
- Augmented state graph: (node, hops)
- Dijkstra with 2D dist and predecessor tracking
- Path reconstruction from (node, hops) chain
- Time/space: O((N*H + M*H) log(N*H))

## Code Example

```javascript
function shortestPathWithHops(graph, S, T, H) {
  // graph: {u: [{to,w}, ...], ...}
  const dist = new Map();
  const prev = new Map();
  // min-heap assumed available: push({time, node, hops})
  const heap = new MinHeap((a,b)=>a.time-b.time);
  dist.set(`${S}|0`, 0);
  heap.push({time:0, node:S, hops:0});
  while (!heap.isEmpty()) {
    const {time,u,k} = heap.pop();
    if (time !== dist.get(`${u}|${k}`)) continue;
    for (const {to:v, w} of (graph[u] || [])) {
      const nk = k + 1;
      if (nk > H) continue;
      const nd = time + w;
      const key = `${v}|${nk}`;
      if (nd < (dist.get(key) ?? Infinity)) {
        dist.set(key, nd);
        prev.set(key, `${u}|${k}`);
        heap.push({time: nd, node: v, hops: nk});
      }
    }
  }
  let bestTime = Infinity; let bestKey = null;
  for (let k = 0; k <= H; k++) {
    const key = `${T}|${k}`;
    const d = dist.get(key);
    if (d != null && d < bestTime) { bestTime = d; bestKey = key; }
  }
  const path = [];
  if (bestKey) {
    let cur = bestKey;
    while (cur) {
      const [node] = cur.split('|');
      path.push(node);
      cur = prev.get(cur);
    }
    path.reverse();
  }
  return { time: bestTime, path };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle multiple equal shortest paths?
- How would you optimize memory for very large graphs?
- How would you adapt if hops constraint is on edges vs. nodes?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses interval DP, proper subproblem decomposition, and practical optimization with prefix sums. Builds intuition for product costs over contiguous blocks.

## Key Concepts
- Interval DP on [i, j]
- Prefix sums for O(1) range sums
- Bottom-up filling by increasing length; base case 0 for single element

## Code Example
```javascript
function minMergeCost(stones){
  const n = stones.length;
  const pref = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++) pref[i+1] = pref[i] + stones[i];
  const sum = (i,j) => pref[j+1]-pref[i];
  const dp = Array.from({length:n}, ()=> Array(n).fill(0));
  for(let len=2; len<=n; len++){
    for(let i=0; i+len-1<n; i++){
      const j = i+len-1;
      let best = Infinity;
      for(let k=i; k<j; k++){
        const cost = dp[i][k] + dp[k+1][j] + sum(i,j);
        if(cost < best) best = cost;
      }
      dp[i][j] = best;
    }
  }
  return n>0 ? dp[0][n-1] : 0;
}
```

